OL,3,GNEWSAStorm Boelo brings disruption
OL,4,Aacross island of Ireland
OL,5,
OL,6,FStorm Boelo has brought gusts of more
OL,7,Fthan 70mph (113kph) to the east coast
OL,8,Fof Northern Ireland, with some of the
OL,9,Fstrongest winds expected overnight.
OL,11,FSome sporting events and Halloween
OL,12,Ffireworks displays have been cancelled,
OL,13,Fflights and ferries disrupted, and the
OL,14,FFoyle bridge in Londonderry is closed
OL,15,Fin both directions.
OL,17,FAn amber warning is in force across
OL,18,Fparts of Antrim and Derry until 10:00
OL,19,FGMT on Sunday, but winds will only
OL,20,Fgradually ease after that, especially
OL,21,Faround coastal and exposed areas.
OL,23,APub: 24-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
FL,413,410,260,120,0,100
